\paragraph{Detector signal semantics.}
The method requires a discriminative detector: both generative alternatives (GPT-2 PPL at AUC\,=\,0.91, $\Delta{=}{+}0.10$; N-gram PPL at AUC\,=\,0.73, $\Delta{=}{+}0.13$) reverse the advantage despite GPT-2's high AUC, because they conflate predictability with synthetic origin and assign high $q$-scores to fluent human text.
TF-IDF+LR (AUC\,=\,0.94, ECE\,=\,0.048) succeeds because its features target provenance rather than fluency.

